<title>GERMANY: TABLE - BASF DETAILS H1 1997 RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TABLE - BASF DETAILS H1 1997 RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net income after taxes	   1,417   vs 1,370</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     2,458   vs 2,323</p>
<p>    Group income from operations	   2,497   vs 2,339</p>
<p>(by location of companies)</p>
<p>     Europe					2,071   vs 1,706</p>
<p>     thereof Germany			   1,306   vs 1,098</p>
<p>     North America			     293     vs 639</p>
<p>     South America			     77	vs -63</p>
<p>     Asia, Pacific Area, Africa	    56	vs 57</p>
<p>(by segment)</p>
<p>     Health &amp; Nutrition			678     vs 718</p>
<p>     Colorants &amp; Finishing Products	411     vs 175</p>
<p>     Chemicals				   817     vs 750</p>
<p>     Plastics &amp; Fibres			 260     vs 457</p>
<p>     Oil &amp; Gas				   482     vs 292</p>
<p>     Other					 -151    vs -53</p>
<p>of which costs of exploratory</p>
<p>     research				    128     vs 99</p>
<p>    Group net sales			    27,797  vs 24,267</p>
<p>(by segment)</p>
<p>     Health &amp; Nutrition			6,062   up 19.9 pct</p>
<p>     Colorants &amp; Finishing Products	6,427   up 14.8 pct</p>
<p>     Chemicals				   4,172   up 15.6 pct</p>
<p>     Plastics &amp; Fibres			 6,878   up 16.6 pct</p>
<p>     Oil &amp; Gas				   3,027   up 32.5 pct</p>
<p>     Other					 1,231   down 32.5 pct</p>
<p>(by location of customers)</p>
<p>     Europe					17,095  up 12.7 pct</p>
<p>     of which Germany			  7,136   up 12.5 pct</p>
<p>     North America			     5,939   up 19.1 pct</p>
<p>     South America			     1,462   up 10.3 pct</p>
<p>     Asia, Pacific Area, Africa	    3,301   up 18.4 pct</p>
<p>(by location of companies)</p>
<p>     Europe					19,394  vs 17,402</p>
<p>     of which Germany			  13,135  vs 11.846</p>
<p>     North America			     5,938   vs 4,849</p>
<p>     South America			     1,092   vs 938</p>
<p>     Asia, Pacific Area, Africa	    1,373   vs 1,078</p>
<p>    Capital expenditures		     1,612   vs 1,417</p>
<p>    Personnel expense			  5,234   vs 4,961</p>
<p>    No of employees (30.6)		   102,336 vs 105,408</p>
<p>    Parent income from operations	  825     vs 875</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax profit		    1,225   vs 1,156</p>
<p>    Parent net sales			   11,950  vs 10,389</p>
<p>    Capital expenditures		     393     vs 419</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German chemical group is BASF AG. Group personnel expense figure does not include pension benefits. The group net sales figures are without petroleum and natural gas taxes.</p>
